1
00:00:00,129 --> 00:00:03,870
There is no audience here tonight in this hall at the National Constitution Center.
今晚在国家宪法中心的这个大厅里没有观众。

2
00:00:03,910 --> 00:00:07,251
This is an intimate setting for two candidates who have never met.
这是一个亲密的环境，适合两位从未见过面的候选人。

3
00:00:07,551 --> 00:00:09,311
President Trump won the coin toss.
特朗普总统赢得了抛硬币的机会。

4
00:00:09,331 --> 00:00:12,052
He chose to deliver the final closing statement of the evening.
他选择在今晚进行最后的总结发言。

5
00:00:12,372 --> 00:00:14,713
Vice President Harris selected the podium to the right.
哈里斯副总统选择了右侧的讲台。

6
00:00:15,053 --> 00:00:17,093
So let's now welcome the candidates to the stage.
现在让我们欢迎候选人上台。

7
00:00:17,173 --> 00:00:20,094
Vice President Kamala Harris and President Donald Trump.
哈里斯副总统和特朗普总统。

8
00:00:27,798 --> 00:00:29,909
Kamala Harris, let's have a good debate.
卡马拉·哈里斯，让我们进行一场良好的辩论。

9
00:00:29,929 --> 00:00:30,251
Thank you.
谢谢你。

10
00:00:32,702 --> 00:00:33,483
Welcome to you both.
欢迎你们两位。

11
00:00:33,623 --> 00:00:34,503
It's wonderful to have you.
很高兴你们在这里。

12
00:00:34,543 --> 00:00:35,964
It's an honor to have you both here tonight.
今晚能有你们两位在此真是荣幸。

13
00:00:36,204 --> 00:00:36,825
Good evening.
晚上好。

14
00:00:36,905 --> 00:00:39,807
We are looking forward to a spirited and thoughtful debate.
我们期待一场热烈而深思熟虑的辩论。

15
00:00:40,247 --> 00:00:41,028
So let's get started.
那么，让我们开始吧。

16
00:00:41,488 --> 00:00:48,353
I want to begin tonight with the issue that voters repeatedly say is their number one issue, and that is the economy and the cost of living in this country.
我想今晚从选民们一再表示的首要问题开始，那就是这个国家的经济和生活成本。

17
00:00:48,853 --> 00:00:58,119
Vice President Harris, you and President Trump were elected four years ago, and your opponent on the stage here tonight often asks his supporters, are you better off than you were four years ago?
哈里斯副总统，你和特朗普总统四年前当选，你的对手今晚在这里常常问他的支持者，你们比四年前过得更好吗？

18
00:00:58,619 --> 00:01:02,542
When it comes to the economy, do you believe Americans are better off than they were four years ago?
在经济方面，你认为美国人比四年前过得更好吗？

19
00:01:03,603 --> 00:01:14,576
So, I was raised as a middle class kid, and I am actually the only person on this stage who has a plan that is about lifting up the middle class and working people of America.
我是在中产阶级家庭长大的，我实际上是这个舞台上唯一一个有计划来提升美国中产阶级和工人阶级的人。

20
00:01:15,357 --> 00:01:20,042
I believe in the ambition, the aspirations, the dreams of the American people.
我相信美国人民的雄心、愿望和梦想。

21
00:01:20,603 --> 00:01:26,048
And that is why I imagine and have actually a plan to build what I call an opportunity economy.
这就是为什么我设想并且实际上有一个计划来建立我所称的机会经济。

22
00:01:26,068 --> 00:01:27,269
Because here's the thing.
因为事情是这样的。

23
00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:31,373
We know that we have a shortage of homes and housing.
我们知道我们面临住房和房屋短缺的问题。

24
00:01:31,873 --> 00:01:34,696
And the cost of housing is too expensive for far too many people.
而住房成本对太多人来说过于昂贵。

25
00:01:35,336 --> 00:01:37,738
We know that young families need support.
我们知道年轻家庭需要支持。

26
00:01:38,579 --> 00:01:55,081
to raise their children, and I intend on extending a tax cut for those families of $6,000, which is the largest child tax credit that we have given in a long time, so that those young families can afford to buy a crib, buy a car seat, buy clothes for their children.
为了抚养孩子，我打算为这些家庭提供6,000美元的减税，这是我们很长时间以来提供的最大儿童税收抵免，以便年轻家庭能够负担得起婴儿床、儿童安全座椅和孩子的衣服。

27
00:01:55,942 --> 00:01:59,425
My passion, one of them, is small businesses.
我的热情之一就是小企业。

28
00:01:59,645 --> 00:02:04,369
I was actually – my mother raised my sister and me, but there was a woman who helped raise us.
实际上，我的母亲养活了我和我的妹妹，但还有一位女性帮助我们成长。

29
00:02:04,449 --> 00:02:05,810
We call her our second mother.
我们称她为我们的第二位母亲。

30
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:07,091
She was a small business owner.
她是一位小企业主。

31
00:02:07,251 --> 00:02:08,652
I love our small businesses.
我热爱我们的中小企业。

32
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:18,340
My plan is to give a $50,000 tax deduction to startup small businesses, knowing they are part of the backbone of America's economy.
我的计划是为初创小企业提供5万美元的税收减免，因为我知道它们是美国经济的支柱之一。

33
00:02:19,061 --> 00:02:22,763
My opponent, on the other hand, his plan is to do what he has done before.
我的对手，另一方面，他的计划就是他以前做过的事情。

34
00:02:23,584 --> 00:02:31,614
which is to provide a tax cut for billionaires and big corporations, which will result in $5 trillion to America's deficit.
那就是为亿万富翁和大企业提供税收减免，这将导致美国的赤字增加5万亿美元。

35
00:02:32,075 --> 00:02:41,807
My opponent has a plan that I call the Trump sales tax, which would be a 20% tax on everyday goods that you rely on to get through the month.
我的对手有一个我称之为特朗普销售税的计划，这将对你们每月依赖的日常商品征收20%的税。

36
00:02:42,748 --> 00:03:01,540
Economists have said that that Trump sales tax would actually result for middle-class families in about $4,000 more a year because of his policies and his ideas about what should be the backs of middle-class people paying for tax cuts for billionaires.
经济学家表示，这项特朗普销售税实际上会让中产阶级家庭每年多花约4000美元，因为他的政策和对中产阶级负担税收减免的看法。

37
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:02,933
President Trump.
特朗普总统。

38
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:20,172
Tariff will be substantial in some cases.
在某些情况下，关税将会很可观。

39
00:03:20,252 --> 00:03:39,550
I took in billions and billions of dollars as you know from China In fact, they never took the tariff off because it was so much money They can't it would totally destroy everything that they've set out to do They're taking in billions of dollars from China and other places They've left the tariffs on when I had it I had tariffs and yet I had no inflation look, we've had a
如你所知，我从中国赚了数十亿的美元，事实上，他们从未取消关税，因为这笔钱太多了，他们无法做到，这将完全摧毁他们所设定的一切。他们从中国和其他地方获得数十亿的收入。

40
00:03:40,291 --> 00:03:44,432
Terrible economy because inflation has which is really known as a country buster.
在我执政时，我有关税，而当时并没有通货膨胀。看看，我们的经济

41
00:03:44,452 --> 00:04:08,839
It breaks up countries We have inflation like very few people have ever seen before probably the worst in our nation's history We were at 21 percent But that's being generous because many things are 50 60 70 and 80 percent higher than they were just a few years ago This has been a disaster for people for the middle class but for every class on top of that we have millions of people pouring into our country from
糟糕，因为通货膨胀，实际上被称为国家破坏者。

42
00:04:09,399 --> 00:04:13,323
prisons and jails from mental institutions and insane asylums.
它摧毁国家。我们有的通货膨胀是前所未见的，可能是我们国家历史上最糟糕的。我们曾达到21%的通货膨胀，但这还是宽容的，因为许多东西的价格比几年前高出50%、60%、70%和80%。

43
00:04:13,784 --> 00:04:21,851
And they're coming in and they're taking jobs that are occupied right now by African Americans and Hispanics and also unions.
这对中产阶级以及所有阶层的人来说都是一场灾难，此外，我们还有数以百万计的人从

44
00:04:21,972 --> 00:04:23,613
Unions are going to be affected very soon.
监狱和精神病院涌入我们的国家。

45
00:04:24,034 --> 00:04:25,075
And you see what's happening.
他们进来后占据了目前由非裔美国人和西班牙裔以及工会成员所占的工作。

46
00:04:25,095 --> 00:04:27,817
You see what's happening with towns throughout the United States.
工会很快就会受到影响。

47
00:04:27,857 --> 00:04:29,799
You look at Springfield, Ohio.
你看到发生了什么。

48
00:04:30,079 --> 00:04:32,362
You look at Aurora in Colorado.
你看到美国各地城镇发生了什么。

49
00:04:32,862 --> 00:04:34,383
They are taking over the towns.
你看看俄亥俄州的斯普林菲尔德。

50
00:04:34,423 --> 00:04:35,744
They're taking over buildings.
你看看科罗拉多州的奥罗拉。

51
00:04:35,784 --> 00:04:37,125
They're going in violently.
他们正在占领这些城镇。

52
00:04:37,506 --> 00:04:44,010
These are the people that she and Biden let into our country, and they're destroying our country.
他们正在占领建筑物。

53
00:04:44,331 --> 00:04:45,271
They're dangerous.
他们以暴力的方式进入。

54
00:04:45,572 --> 00:04:49,294
They're at the highest level of criminality, and we have to get them out.
这些人是她和拜登让进入我们国家的，他们正在摧毁我们的国家。

55
00:04:49,354 --> 00:04:50,495
We have to get them out fast.
他们是危险的。

56
00:04:50,896 --> 00:04:54,638
I created one of the greatest economies in the history of our country.
他们的犯罪率处于最高水平，我们必须把他们赶出去。

57
00:04:55,179 --> 00:04:56,780
I'll do it again and even better.
我们必须迅速把他们赶出去。

58
00:04:56,980 --> 00:05:03,551
We are going to get to immigration and border security during this debate, but I would like to let Vice President Harris respond on the economy here.
我创造了我们国家历史上最伟大的经济之一。

59
00:05:04,022 --> 00:05:05,263
Well, I would love to.
我会再次做到，甚至做得更好。

60
00:05:05,343 --> 00:05:08,605
Let's talk about what Donald Trump left us.
在这场辩论中，我们将讨论移民和边境安全，但我想让哈里斯副总统在经济方面回应一下。

61
00:05:09,345 --> 00:05:14,248
Donald Trump left us the worst unemployment since the Great Depression.
唐纳德·特朗普留下了自大萧条以来最糟糕的失业率。

62
00:05:14,909 --> 00:05:20,552
Donald Trump left us the worst public health epidemic in a century.
唐纳德·特朗普留下了一个世纪以来最严重的公共卫生疫情。

63
00:05:21,072 --> 00:05:27,917
Donald Trump left us the worst attack on our democracy since the Civil War.
唐纳德·特朗普留下了自内战以来对我们民主的最严重攻击。

64
00:05:28,877 --> 00:05:32,061
And what we have done is clean up Donald Trump's mess.
我们所做的就是清理唐纳德·特朗普留下的烂摊子。

65
00:05:32,681 --> 00:05:39,088
What we have done and what I intend to do is build on what we know are the aspirations and the hopes of the American people.
我们所做的以及我打算做的，就是在美国人民的愿望和希望的基础上继续努力。

66
00:05:39,108 --> 00:05:44,333
But I'm going to tell you on this debate tonight, you're going to hear from the same old tired playbook.
但我想告诉你，今晚的辩论中，你会听到同样老套的剧本。

67
00:05:45,234 --> 00:05:48,298
A bunch of lies, grievances, and name-calling.
一堆谎言、抱怨和人身攻击。

68
00:05:48,778 --> 00:05:59,030
What you're going to hear tonight is a detailed and dangerous plan called Project 2025 that the former president intends on implementing if he were elected again.
你今晚要听到的是一个详细而危险的计划，叫做项目2025，前总统打算在再次当选后实施。

69
00:06:00,171 --> 00:06:10,640
I believe very strongly that the American people want a president who understands the importance of bringing us together, knowing we have so much more in common than what separates us.
我非常坚信，美国人民想要一位理解团结重要性的总统，知道我们之间有更多共同点，而不是分歧。

70
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:14,042
And I pledge to you to be a president for all Americans.
我向你们承诺，我会成为所有美国人的总统。

71
00:06:14,243 --> 00:06:15,744
President Trump will give you a minute here to respond.
特朗普总统将在这里给你一分钟的时间回应。

72
00:06:16,044 --> 00:06:21,308
Number one, I have nothing to do, as you know, and as she knows better than anyone, I have nothing to do with Project 2025.
首先，正如你所知道的，以及她比任何人都更清楚的，我与项目2025毫无关系。

73
00:06:22,529 --> 00:06:23,290
That's out there.
这件事是公开的。

74
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:24,351
I haven't read it.
我没有读过它。

75
00:06:24,531 --> 00:06:25,952
I don't want to read it purposely.
我故意不想读它。

76
00:06:25,992 --> 00:06:26,872
I'm not going to read it.
我不会读它。

77
00:06:27,193 --> 00:06:28,854
This was a group of people that got together.
这是一个聚集在一起的人群。

78
00:06:28,914 --> 00:06:33,217
They came up with some ideas, I guess some good, some bad, but it makes no difference.
他们提出了一些想法，我想有些好，有些坏，但这没什么区别。

79
00:06:33,257 --> 00:06:34,178
I have nothing to do.
我与此无关。

80
00:06:34,298 --> 00:06:35,659
Everybody knows I'm an open book.
大家都知道我是一开放的书籍。

81
00:06:35,739 --> 00:06:37,120
Everybody knows what I'm going to do.
大家都知道我会做什么。

82
00:06:37,181 --> 00:06:41,444
Cut taxes very substantially and create a great economy like I did before.
大幅减税，创造一个像我之前那样的伟大经济。

83
00:06:41,964 --> 00:06:43,365
We had the greatest economy.
我们曾拥有最伟大的经济。

84
00:06:43,405 --> 00:06:44,685
We got hit with a pandemic.
我们遭遇了疫情。

85
00:06:45,065 --> 00:06:49,807
And the pandemic was not since 1917, where 100 million people died.
而这场疫情自1917年以来，造成了一亿人死亡。

86
00:06:50,187 --> 00:06:51,328
Has there been anything like it?
有没有类似的事情发生过？

87
00:06:51,388 --> 00:06:53,589
We did a phenomenal job with the pandemic.
我们在疫情期间做得非常出色。

88
00:06:54,049 --> 00:07:01,692
We handed them over a country where the economy and where the stock market was higher than it was before the pandemic came in.
我们交给他们一个经济和股市都高于疫情之前的国家。

89
00:07:02,252 --> 00:07:03,872
Nobody's ever seen anything like it.
没有人见过这样的事情。

90
00:07:04,253 --> 00:07:06,553
We made ventilators for the entire world.
我们为全世界制造了呼吸机。

91
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:07,454
We got gowns.
我们有礼服。

92
00:07:07,514 --> 00:07:08,394
We got masks.
我们有口罩。

93
00:07:08,454 --> 00:07:10,335
We did things that nobody thought possible.
我们做了许多没人认为可能的事情。

94
00:07:10,815 --> 00:07:13,136
And people give me credit for rebuilding the military.
人们称赞我重建了军队。

95
00:07:13,156 --> 00:07:17,939
They give me credit for a lot of things, but not enough credit for the great job we did with the pandemic.
他们称赞我很多事情，但对我们在疫情期间所做的伟大工作却没有给予足够的认可。

96
00:07:18,239 --> 00:07:20,561
But the only jobs they got were bounce-back jobs.
但他们得到的工作只是反弹性工作。

97
00:07:20,581 --> 00:07:24,823
These were jobs bounce-back, and it bounced back and it went to their benefit.
这些是反弹性工作，反弹了，最终对他们有利。

98
00:07:25,183 --> 00:07:26,844
But I was the one that created them.
但我是创造这些工作的那个人。

99
00:07:26,964 --> 00:07:28,705
They know it, and so does everybody else.
他们知道这一点，其他人也是如此。

100
00:07:28,805 --> 00:07:29,986
Vice President Harris, I'll let you respond.
副总统哈里斯，我让你回应。

101
00:07:32,662 --> 00:07:34,163
Donald Trump has no plan for you.
唐纳德·特朗普没有为你制定任何计划。

102
00:07:35,304 --> 00:07:39,947
And when you look at his economic plan, it's all about tax breaks for the richest people.
当你看看他的经济计划时，完全是为富人减税。

103
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:52,157
I am offering what I describe as an opportunity economy, and the best economists in our country, if not the world, have reviewed our relative plans for the future of America.
我提供的是我所描述的机会经济，国内外最优秀的经济学家审视了我们对美国未来的相对计划。

104
00:07:52,877 --> 00:08:00,043
What Goldman Sachs has said is that Donald Trump's plan would make the economy worse, mine would strengthen the economy.
高盛所说的是，唐纳德·特朗普的计划会使经济更糟，而我的计划会增强经济。

105
00:08:00,484 --> 00:08:06,809
What the Wharton School has said is Donald Trump's plan would actually explode the deficit.
沃顿商学院所说的是，唐纳德·特朗普的计划实际上会导致赤字膨胀。

106
00:08:07,349 --> 00:08:17,378
Sixteen Nobel laureates have described his economic plan as something that would increase inflation and by the middle of next year would invite a recession.
十六位诺贝尔奖得主形容他的经济计划会增加通货膨胀，并且在明年年中将引发衰退。

107
00:08:18,078 --> 00:08:22,024
You just have to look at where we are and where we stand on the issues.
你只需看看我们现在的位置和我们在这些问题上的立场。

108
00:08:22,064 --> 00:08:31,297
And I'd invite you to know that Donald Trump actually has no plan for you, because he is more interested in defending himself than he is in looking out for you.
我想让你们知道，唐纳德·特朗普实际上没有为你制定计划，因为他更关心为自己辩护，而不是为你着想。

109
00:08:32,034 --> 00:08:33,015
It's just a soundbite.
这只是一个口号。

110
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:41,421
They gave her that to say, look, I went to the Wharton School of Finance and many of those professors, the top professors think my plan is a brilliant plan.
他们让她这样说，看看，我去了沃顿商学院，许多顶尖教授认为我的计划是一个杰出的计划。

111
00:08:41,481 --> 00:08:42,221
It's a great plan.
这是一个伟大的计划。

112
00:08:42,301 --> 00:08:46,264
It's a plan that's going to bring up our worth, our value as a country.
这是一个将提升我们国家价值的计划。

113
00:08:46,324 --> 00:08:49,186
It's going to make people want to be able to go and work and
这将使人们愿意去工作，

114
00:08:49,746 --> 00:08:55,011
and create jobs and create a lot of good, solid money for our country.
并创造工作机会，为我们的国家创造大量可靠的财富。

115
00:08:55,512 --> 00:08:58,855
Just to finish off, she doesn't have a plan.
最后，她没有计划。

116
00:08:59,235 --> 00:09:09,465
She copied Biden's plan, and it's like four sentences, like run, spot, run, four sentences that are just, oh, we'll try and lower taxes.
她抄袭了拜登的计划，就像四句话，像“跑，点，跑”，四句话只是哦，我们会努力降低税收。

117
00:09:09,985 --> 00:09:10,806
She doesn't have a plan.
她没有计划。

118
00:09:10,826 --> 00:09:11,647
Take a look at her plan.
看看她的计划。

119
00:09:11,887 --> 00:09:12,828
She doesn't have a plan.
她没有计划。

120
00:09:13,737 --> 00:09:16,199
Mr. President, I do want to drill down on something you both brought up.
总统先生，我确实想深入探讨你们两位提到的一个问题。

121
00:09:16,759 --> 00:09:18,660
The Vice President brought up your tariffs.
副总统提到了您的关税。

122
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:24,904
You responded, and let's drill down on this, because your plan is what she calls is essentially a national sales tax.
您对此做出了回应，让我们深入探讨一下，因为您的计划在她看来本质上是一种国家销售税。

123
00:09:24,944 --> 00:09:28,907
Your proposal calls for tariffs, as you pointed out here, on foreign imports across the board.
正如您在这里指出的，您的提案要求对所有外国进口商品全面征收关税。

124
00:09:28,927 --> 00:09:34,611
You recently said that you might double your plan, imposing tariffs up to 20 percent on goods coming into this country.
您最近表示，您可能会将计划加倍，对进入该国的商品征收高达20%的关税。

125
00:09:35,091 --> 00:09:39,594
As you know, many economists say that with tariffs at that level, costs are then passed on to the consumer.
正如您所知，许多经济学家表示，达到这种水平的关税，成本将最终转嫁给消费者。

126
00:09:40,214 --> 00:09:49,080
Vice President Harris has argued it'll mean higher prices on gas, food, clothing, medication, arguing it costs the typical family nearly $4,000 a year.
副总统哈里斯认为，这将意味着汽油、食品、衣物和药品价格上涨，声称这会使普通家庭每年多花近4000美元。

127
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:52,702
Do you believe Americans can afford higher prices because of tariffs?
您认为美国人能够承受因关税而上涨的价格吗？

128
00:09:52,722 --> 00:09:54,103
They're not going to have higher prices.
他们不会面临更高的价格。

129
00:09:54,143 --> 00:10:00,567
What's going to happen, who's going to have higher prices is China and all of the countries that have been ripping us off for years.
面临更高价格的将是中国以及所有这些多年来一直在剥削我们的国家。

130
00:10:01,107 --> 00:10:03,009
I charge, I was the only president ever,
我敢说，我是唯一一位曾经的总统，

131
00:10:03,709 --> 00:10:08,071
China is paying us hundreds of billions of dollars and so are other countries.
中国向我们支付了数百亿美元，其他国家也是如此。

132
00:10:19,116 --> 00:10:22,397
billions of dollars, hundreds of billions of dollars.
数十亿美元，数百亿美元。

133
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:25,498
I had no inflation, virtually no inflation.
我几乎没有通货膨胀，几乎没有通货膨胀。

134
00:10:25,818 --> 00:10:31,140
They had the highest inflation, perhaps, in the history of our country, because I've never seen a worse period of time.
他们经历的通货膨胀可能是我们国家历史上最高的，因为我从未见过如此糟糕的时期。

135
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:35,421
People can't go out and buy cereal or bacon or eggs or anything else.
人们无法出去买谷物、培根、鸡蛋或其他任何东西。

136
00:10:36,101 --> 00:10:40,764
These the people of our country are absolutely dying with what they've done.
我们国家的人们正因他们所做的事情而痛苦不堪。

137
00:10:41,064 --> 00:10:42,625
They've destroyed the economy.
他们摧毁了经济。

138
00:10:42,926 --> 00:10:44,407
And all you have to do is look at a poll.
您只需看看民调。

139
00:10:44,747 --> 00:10:52,292
The polls say 80 and 85 and even 90 percent that the Trump economy was great, that their economy was terrible.
民调显示，80%、85%甚至90%的人认为特朗普的经济很好，而他们的经济糟糕透顶。

140
00:10:52,452 --> 00:10:54,634
Vice President Harris, I do want to ask for your response.
副总统哈里斯，我想请您回应一下。

141
00:10:54,654 --> 00:11:00,037
And you heard what the president said there, because the Biden administration did keep a number of the Trump tariffs in place.
您听到了总统所说的话，因为拜登政府确实保留了一些特朗普时期的关税。

142
00:11:00,057 --> 00:11:00,738
So how do you respond?
那么您如何回应呢？

143
00:11:01,411 --> 00:11:08,996
Well, let's be clear that the Trump administration resulted in a trade deficit, one of the highest we've ever seen in the history of America.
首先要明确的是，特朗普政府导致了贸易逆差，这是我们美国历史上最高的之一。

144
00:11:09,677 --> 00:11:11,117
He invited trade wars.
他引发了贸易战。

145
00:11:11,398 --> 00:11:20,564
You want to talk about his deal with China, what he ended up doing is under Donald Trump's presidency, he ended up selling American chips
您想谈谈他与中国的交易，实际上在特朗普总统任期内，他最终向中国出售了美国芯片

146
00:11:21,004 --> 00:11:35,060
to China to help them improve and modernize their military basically sold us out when a policy about China should be in making sure the United States of America wins the competition for the 21st century.
以帮助他们改善和现代化他们的军队，基本上是出卖了我们，而关于中国的政策应该是确保美国在21世纪的竞争中获胜。

147
00:11:36,201 --> 00:11:57,758
which means focusing on the details of what that requires, focusing on relationships with our allies, focusing on investing in American-based technology so that we win the race on AI, on quantum computing, focusing on what we need to do to support America's workforce so that we don't end up having, on the short end of the stick,
这意味着关注实现这一目标所需的细节，关注与我们的盟友的关系，关注投资美国本土技术，以便我们在人工智能、量子计算的竞赛中获胜，关注我们需要做些什么来支持美国的劳动力，以免我们在

148
00:11:58,298 --> 00:12:00,160
in terms of workers' rights.
工人权益方面处于劣势。

149
00:12:00,561 --> 00:12:08,909
But what Donald Trump did—let's talk about this—with COVID is he actually thanked President Xi for what he did during COVID.
但特朗普所做的——让我们谈谈这一点——在COVID期间，他实际上感谢了习近平主席在COVID期间所做的事情。

150
00:12:08,929 --> 00:12:09,810
Look at his tweet.
看看他的推特。

151
00:12:10,210 --> 00:12:13,193
Thank you, President Xi!
谢谢你，习近平总统！

152
00:12:13,813 --> 00:12:21,341
When we know that Xi was responsible for lacking and not giving us transparency about the origins of COVID.
当我们知道习近平对COVID起源缺乏透明度并未告知我们时。

153
00:12:21,684 --> 00:12:22,624
President Trump, I'll let you respond.
特朗普总统，我让你回应。

154
00:12:22,644 --> 00:12:25,505
First of all, they bought their chips from Taiwan.
首先，他们从台湾购买了芯片。

155
00:12:25,726 --> 00:12:32,168
We hardly make chips anymore because of philosophies like they have and policies like they have.
由于他们的理念和政策，我们几乎不再制造芯片了。

156
00:12:32,268 --> 00:12:34,209
I don't say her because she has no policy.
我不说她，因为她没有政策。

157
00:12:34,629 --> 00:12:39,171
Everything that she believed three years ago and four years ago is out the window.
她三年前和四年前相信的一切都已经抛到脑后。

158
00:12:39,531 --> 00:12:41,011
She's going to my philosophy now.
她现在转向我的理念。

159
00:12:41,051 --> 00:12:42,752
In fact, I was going to send her a MAGA hat.
事实上，我本来想给她寄一顶MAGA帽。

160
00:12:43,232 --> 00:12:44,493
She's gone to my philosophy.
她已经转向我的理念。

161
00:12:45,433 --> 00:12:50,075
If she ever got elected, she'd change it, and it will be the end of our country.
如果她当选，她会改变，这将是我们国家的终结。

162
00:12:50,476 --> 00:12:51,396
She's a Marxist.
她是一个马克思主义者。

163
00:12:51,576 --> 00:12:52,957
Everybody knows she's a Marxist.
大家都知道她是一个马克思主义者。

164
00:12:53,217 --> 00:12:57,459
Her father's a Marxist professor in economics, and he taught her well.
她的父亲是一位马克思主义经济学教授，他教得很好。

165
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:09,766
But when you look at what she's done to our country, and when you look at these millions and millions of people that are pouring into our country monthly, where it's, I believe, 21 million people, not the 15 that people say,
但是当你看看她对我们国家所做的，以及每月涌入我们国家的数百万人民时，我相信是2100万人，而不是大家说的1500万，

166
00:13:10,126 --> 00:13:11,806
And I think it's a lot higher than the 21.
我认为实际数字远高于2100万。

167
00:13:12,447 --> 00:13:14,607
That's bigger than New York State pouring in.
这比纽约州还要多。

168
00:13:14,927 --> 00:13:17,108
And just look at what they're doing to our country.
看看他们对我们国家做了什么。

169
00:13:17,508 --> 00:13:18,328
They're criminals.
他们是罪犯。

170
00:13:18,428 --> 00:13:20,269
Many of these people coming in are criminals.
许多进入的人是罪犯。

171
00:13:20,649 --> 00:13:22,589
And that's bad for our economy, too.
这对我们的经济也不好。

172
00:13:22,629 --> 00:13:24,910
You know, you mentioned before, we'll talk about immigration later.
你之前提到，我们稍后会谈到移民问题。

173
00:13:25,250 --> 00:13:28,651
Well, bad immigration is the worst thing that can happen to our economy.
糟糕的移民是对我们经济最糟糕的事情。

174
00:13:29,571 --> 00:13:35,744
They have, and she has, destroyed our country with policy that's insane.
他们有，她有，以疯狂的政策摧毁了我们的国家。

175
00:13:36,085 --> 00:13:39,291
Almost policy that you'd say they have to hate our country.
几乎可以说是恨我们的国家的政策。

176
00:13:39,411 --> 00:13:40,454
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢你。

177
00:13:40,594 --> 00:13:40,774
Lindsey?
林赛？

178
00:13:41,377 --> 00:13:43,398
I want to turn to the issue of abortion.
我想转向堕胎问题。

179
00:13:43,518 --> 00:13:47,841
President Trump, you've often touted that you were able to kill Roe v. Wade last year.
特朗普总统，你经常夸耀自己去年能够推翻《罗诉韦德》。

180
00:13:47,921 --> 00:13:52,564
You said that you were proud to be the most pro-life president in American history.
你说你为成为美国历史上最支持生命的总统而感到自豪。

181
00:13:52,965 --> 00:13:57,868
Then last month, you said that your administration would be great for women and their reproductive rights.
上个月，你表示你的政府将对女性及其生育权利非常有利。

182
00:13:58,248 --> 00:14:05,272
In your home state of Florida, you surprised many with regard to your six-week abortion ban, because you initially had said that it was too short.
在你家乡佛罗里达州，你在六周堕胎禁令方面让许多人感到惊讶，因为你最初曾表示这段时间太短。

183
00:14:05,313 --> 00:14:09,075
And you said, quote, I'm going to be voting that we need more than six weeks.
你曾说过，引用：“我将投票支持我们需要超过六周的时间。”

184
00:14:09,155 --> 00:14:14,380
But then, the very next day, you reversed course and said you would vote to support the six-week ban.
但就在第二天，你却改变了立场，表示你将投票支持六周禁令。

185
00:14:15,001 --> 00:14:22,349
Vice President Harris says that women shouldn't trust you on the issue of abortion because you've changed your position so many times.
哈里斯副总统表示，女性在堕胎问题上不应该信任你，因为你改变立场的次数太多。

186
00:14:22,749 --> 00:14:24,511
Therefore, why should they trust you?
那么，她们为什么应该信任你呢？

187
00:14:24,551 --> 00:14:32,060
The reason I'm doing that vote is because the plan is, as you know, the voters, they have abortion in the ninth month.
我投票的原因是因为，正如你所知，选民们在第九个月就有堕胎的情况。

188
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:42,052
They even have and you can look at the governor of West Virginia, the previous governor of West Virginia, not the current governor is doing an excellent job, but the governor before he said
你甚至可以看看西弗吉尼亚州的前州长，而不是现任州长，他做得非常好，但之前的州长曾说过：

189
00:14:42,452 --> 00:14:45,736
The baby will be born, and we will decide what to do with the baby.
“婴儿将会出生，我们将决定如何处理这个婴儿。”

190
00:14:45,776 --> 00:14:47,418
In other words, we'll execute the baby.
换句话说，我们将处决这个婴儿。

191
00:14:47,779 --> 00:14:50,622
And that's why I did that, because that predominates.
这就是我这么做的原因，因为这种观点占主导地位。

192
00:14:50,822 --> 00:14:51,804
Because they're radical.
因为他们是激进的。

193
00:14:51,844 --> 00:14:53,566
The Democrats are radical in that.
民主党在这方面是激进的。

194
00:14:53,966 --> 00:15:00,695
And her vice presidential pick, which I think is a horrible pick, by the way, for our country, because he is really out of it.
而她的副总统人选，我认为是对我们国家一个可怕的选择，因为他真的不在状态。

195
00:15:01,235 --> 00:15:06,598
But her vice presidential pick says abortion in the ninth month is absolutely fine.
但她的副总统人选表示，第九个月的堕胎绝对没问题。

196
00:15:06,838 --> 00:15:14,283
He also says execution after birth, it's execution, no longer abortion because the baby is born, is okay.
他还表示，出生后的处决——这已经不再是堕胎，因为婴儿已经出生——是可以的。

197
00:15:14,703 --> 00:15:16,905
And that's not okay with me, hence the vote.
这对我来说是不可接受的，因此我投了票。

198
00:15:17,245 --> 00:15:18,986
But what I did is something for
但我所做的是，

199
00:15:20,247 --> 00:15:23,932
52 years they've been trying to get Roe v. Wade into the states.
52年来，他们一直在努力将《罗诉韦德案》引入各州。

200
00:15:24,693 --> 00:15:34,427
And through the genius and heart and strength of six Supreme Court justices, we were able to do that.
通过六位最高法院法官的智慧、勇气和力量，我们能够做到这一点。

201
00:15:34,467 --> 00:15:36,190
Now, I believe in the exceptions for
现在，我相信对强奸、乱伦和母亲生命的例外。

202
00:15:36,650 --> 00:15:38,732
rape, incest, and life of the mother.
我对此坚信不疑。

203
00:15:38,832 --> 00:15:39,873
I believe strongly in it.
罗纳德·里根也是这样认为的。

204
00:15:39,933 --> 00:15:41,054
Ronald Reagan did also.
85%的共和党人也支持例外。

205
00:15:41,435 --> 00:15:43,196
Eighty-five percent of Republicans do.
例外。

206
00:15:43,757 --> 00:15:44,378
Exceptions.
非常重要。

207
00:15:44,458 --> 00:15:45,258
Very important.
但我们能够做到，现在各州正在对其进行投票。

208
00:15:45,699 --> 00:15:49,162
But we were able to get it, and now states are voting on it.
这是第一次，你将看到——看，这是一个在过去52年里撕裂我们国家的问题。

209
00:15:49,523 --> 00:15:55,729
And for the first time, you're going to see — look, this is an issue that's torn our country apart for 52 years.
每一位法律学者、每一位民主党人、每一位共和党人、自由派、保守派，他们都希望这个问题能重新带回各州，让人民投票。

210
00:15:57,390 --> 00:16:06,314
Every legal scholar, every Democrat, every Republican, liberal, conservative, they all wanted this issue to be brought back to the states where the people could vote.
这是一个我们国家的基本问题。

211
00:16:06,794 --> 00:16:08,295
And that's what happened.
这就是发生的事情

212
00:16:08,495 --> 00:16:11,636
Now, Ohio, the vote was somewhat liberal.
现在，俄亥俄州的投票结果稍微偏向自由派

213
00:16:12,196 --> 00:16:15,918
Kansas, the vote was somewhat liberal, much more liberal than people would have thought.
堪萨斯州的投票结果也稍微偏向自由派，比人们想象的要自由得多

214
00:16:16,318 --> 00:16:18,239
But each individual state
但每个州

215
00:16:18,619 --> 00:16:19,420
is voting.
都在投票

216
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,901
It's the vote of the people now.
现在是人民的投票

217
00:16:20,941 --> 00:16:22,662
It's not tied up in the federal government.
这与联邦政府无关

218
00:16:23,042 --> 00:16:24,503
I did a great service in doing it.
我在这方面做了很大的贡献

219
00:16:24,523 --> 00:16:25,503
It took courage to do it.
这样做需要勇气

220
00:16:25,804 --> 00:16:28,305
And the Supreme Court had great courage in doing it.
最高法院也展现了巨大的勇气

221
00:16:28,645 --> 00:16:31,527
And I give tremendous credit to those six justices.
我对那六位法官给予了极大的赞誉

222
00:16:31,888 --> 00:16:36,050
There is no state in this country where it is legal to kill a baby after it's born.
在这个国家，没有一个州允许在婴儿出生后杀死婴儿

223
00:16:36,450 --> 00:16:38,992
Madam Vice President, I want to get your response to President Trump.
副总统女士，我想听听您对特朗普总统的回应

224
00:16:39,112 --> 00:16:43,575
Well, as I said, you're going to hear a bunch of lies, and that's not actually a surprising fact.
好吧，正如我所说的，您将听到一堆谎言，这并不是一个令人惊讶的事实

225
00:16:44,716 --> 00:16:45,996
Let's understand how we got here.
让我们理解一下我们是如何走到这一步的

226
00:16:46,997 --> 00:16:54,919
Donald Trump hand-selected three members of the United States Supreme Court with the intention that they would undo the protections of Roe v. Wade.
唐纳德·特朗普精心挑选了三位美国最高法院的法官，目的是为了撤销《罗诉韦德案》的保护

227
00:16:55,839 --> 00:16:58,039
And they did exactly as he intended.
他们确实如他所愿地做了

228
00:16:58,439 --> 00:17:08,921
And now in over 20 states, there are Trump abortion bans, which make it criminal for a doctor or nurse to provide health care.
现在在超过20个州，特朗普的堕胎禁令使医生或护士提供医疗服务成为犯罪

229
00:17:09,061 --> 00:17:11,502
In one state, it provides prison for life.
在一个州，刑罚是终身监禁

230
00:17:12,762 --> 00:17:18,108
Trump abortion bans that make no exception even for rape and incest, which understand what that means.
特朗普的堕胎禁令甚至对强奸和乱伦没有例外，想想这意味着什么

231
00:17:18,609 --> 00:17:26,758
A survivor of a crime, a violation to their body, does not have the right to make a decision about what happens to their body next.
犯罪的幸存者，身体的侵犯者，没有权利决定自己身体接下来发生什么

232
00:17:26,818 --> 00:17:27,919
That is immoral.
这是不道德的

233
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:35,106
And one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree.
人们不必放弃他们的信仰或深信的信念来同意这一点

234
00:17:35,507 --> 00:17:41,933
The government, and Donald Trump certainly, should not be telling a woman what to do with her body.
政府，尤其是唐纳德·特朗普，绝不应该告诉女性该如何处理自己的身体

235
00:17:42,133 --> 00:17:44,996
I have talked with women around our country.
我与全国各地的女性进行了交谈

236
00:17:45,416 --> 00:17:47,718
You want to talk about this is what people wanted?
您想谈谈这就是人们想要的？

237
00:17:48,559 --> 00:18:02,325
Pregnant women who want to carry a pregnancy to term, suffering from a miscarriage, being denied care in an emergency room because the health care providers are afraid they might go to jail, and she's bleeding out in a car in the parking lot.
怀孕的女性想要将妊娠维持到足月，却因流产而在急救室被拒绝治疗，因为医疗提供者害怕他们可能会入狱，而她在停车场的车里出血

238
00:18:02,906 --> 00:18:03,766
She didn't want that.
她不想那样

239
00:18:04,186 --> 00:18:06,727
Her husband didn't want that.
她的丈夫也不想那样

240
00:18:06,767 --> 00:18:12,150
A 12 or 13-year-old survivor of incest being forced to carry a pregnancy to term.
一个12或13岁的乱伦幸存者被迫将妊娠维持到足月

241
00:18:12,890 --> 00:18:13,951
They don't want that.
他们不想要这个。

242
00:18:15,239 --> 00:18:27,607
And I pledge to you, when Congress passes a bill to put back in place the protections of Roe v. Wade as President of the United States, I will proudly sign it into law.
我向你们承诺，当国会通过一项法案恢复《罗诉韦德案》的保护时，作为美国总统，我将自豪地签署它成为法律。

243
00:18:27,927 --> 00:18:33,671
But understand, if Donald Trump were to be reelected, he will sign a national abortion ban.
但请明白，如果唐纳德·特朗普再次当选，他将签署一项全国性堕胎禁令。

244
00:18:34,012 --> 00:18:42,337
Understand, in his Project 2025, there would be a national abortion monitor that would be monitoring your pregnancies, your miscarriages.
要理解，在他的《2025计划》中，将设立一个全国堕胎监测机构，监控你的怀孕和流产情况。

245
00:18:42,737 --> 00:18:44,699
I think the American people believe
我认为美国人民相信

246
00:18:45,419 --> 00:18:52,951
that certain freedoms, in particular the freedom to make decisions about one's own body, should not be made by the government.
某些自由，尤其是关于个人身体决策的自由，不应由政府来决定。

247
00:18:53,311 --> 00:18:55,074
Thank you, Vice President Harris.
谢谢你，哈里斯副总统。

248
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,296
Well, there she goes again.
好吧，她又来了。

249
00:18:56,536 --> 00:18:57,157
It's a lie.
这是谎言。

250
00:18:57,778 --> 00:19:00,983
I'm not signing a ban and there's no reason to sign a ban because
我不会签署禁令，也没有理由去签署禁令，因为

251
00:19:01,283 --> 00:19:03,284
We've gotten what everybody wanted.
我们得到了每个人想要的东西。

252
00:19:03,685 --> 00:19:10,730
Democrats, Republicans, and everybody else, and every legal scholar wanted it to be brought back into the states.
民主党、共和党以及所有人和每位法律学者都希望这个问题回归各州。

253
00:19:10,850 --> 00:19:12,151
And the states are voting.
各州正在投票。

254
00:19:12,631 --> 00:19:14,012
And it may take a little time.
这可能需要一些时间。

255
00:19:14,472 --> 00:19:19,436
But for 52 years, this issue has torn our country apart.
但在过去的52年里，这个问题撕裂了我们的国家。

256
00:19:19,816 --> 00:19:21,718
And they've wanted it back in the states.
他们希望这个问题回归各州。

257
00:19:21,838 --> 00:19:24,420
And I did something that nobody thought was possible.
而我做了一件没人认为可能的事情。

258
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:26,481
The states are now voting.
各州现在正在投票。

259
00:19:27,081 --> 00:19:29,522
What she says is an absolute lie.
她所说的完全是谎言。

260
00:19:29,962 --> 00:19:38,567
And as far as the abortion ban, no, I'm not in favor of abortion ban, but it doesn't matter because this issue has now been taken over by the states.
至于堕胎禁令，不，我不支持堕胎禁令，但这并不重要，因为这个问题现在已经由各州接管。

261
00:19:38,647 --> 00:19:41,048
Would you veto a national abortion ban if it came to your desk?
如果一项全国堕胎禁令送到你面前，你会否决吗？

262
00:19:41,068 --> 00:19:43,449
Well, I won't have to because, again, two things.
好吧，我不会，因为再说两件事。

263
00:19:43,709 --> 00:19:45,510
Number one, she said she'll go back to Congress.
第一，她说她会回到国会。

264
00:19:45,530 --> 00:19:46,410
She'll never get the vote.
她永远无法获得投票。

265
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:54,172
It's impossible for her to get the vote, especially now with the 50-50, essentially 50-50 in both Senate and the House.
她根本不可能获得投票，尤其是在参议院和众议院基本上是50-50的情况下。

266
00:19:54,672 --> 00:19:55,613
She's not going to get the vote.
她不会得到投票。

267
00:19:55,873 --> 00:19:56,573
She can't get the vote.
她无法获得投票。

268
00:19:56,593 --> 00:19:57,853
She won't even come close to it.
她甚至不会接近这个。

269
00:19:57,874 --> 00:19:58,594
So it's just talk.
所以这只是空谈。

270
00:19:58,894 --> 00:19:59,914
You know what it reminds me of?
你知道这让我想起什么吗？

271
00:19:59,954 --> 00:20:05,056
When they said they're going to get student loans terminated, and it ended up being a total catastrophe.
当他们说要取消学生贷款时，结果却完全是一场灾难。

272
00:20:05,836 --> 00:20:05,996
This is
这就是

273
00:20:22,442 --> 00:20:32,891
taunted with this whole thing about this whole idea and how unfair that would have been part of the reason they lost to The millions and millions of people that had to pay off their student loans.
被嘲笑的整个事情，以及这种想法有多么不公平，这可能是他们输给那些必须偿还学生贷款的数百万人的部分原因。

274
00:20:33,152 --> 00:20:39,177
They didn't get it for free But they were saying it's the same way that they talked about that that they talk about abortion.
他们并不是免费的，但他们的说法就像他们谈论堕胎时所说的一样。

275
00:20:39,457 --> 00:20:42,620
But if I could just get a yes or no, because you're running me, J.D.
但如果我能得到一个是或不是的回答，因为你在逼我，J.D.

276
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:45,963
Vance has said that you would veto if it did come to your desk.
范斯说如果它真的到了你的办公桌上，你会否决它。

277
00:20:45,983 --> 00:20:47,865
Well, I didn't discuss it with J.D.
好吧，我没有和J.D.讨论这个。

278
00:20:47,925 --> 00:20:54,912
In all fairness, J.D., and I don't mind if he has a certain view, but I think he was speaking for me, but I really didn't.
公平地说，J.D.，我不介意他有某种观点，但我认为他在为我发言，而我并没有。

279
00:20:56,638 --> 00:20:59,900
We don't have to discuss it, because she'd never be able to get it.
我们不必讨论，因为她根本无法获得批准。

280
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:02,422
Just like she couldn't get student loans, they couldn't get student loans.
就像她无法获得学生贷款一样，他们也无法获得学生贷款。

281
00:21:02,442 --> 00:21:04,264
They didn't even come close to getting student loans.
他们甚至没有接近获得学生贷款。

282
00:21:04,564 --> 00:21:08,267
They taunted young people and a lot of other people that had loans.
他们嘲笑年轻人和许多其他有贷款的人。

283
00:21:08,887 --> 00:21:10,168
They can never get this approved.
他们永远无法获得批准。

284
00:21:10,468 --> 00:21:12,730
So it doesn't matter what she says about going to Congress.
所以她关于去国会的说法无关紧要。

285
00:21:12,810 --> 00:21:13,270
Oh, wonderful.
哦，太好了。

286
00:21:13,290 --> 00:21:14,151
Let's go to Congress.
我们去国会吧。

287
00:21:14,191 --> 00:21:14,411
Do it.
去做吧。

288
00:21:14,931 --> 00:21:19,335
But the fact is that for years, they wanted to get it out of Congress and out of the federal government.
但事实是，多年来，他们想把它从国会和联邦政府中拿出来。

289
00:21:19,675 --> 00:21:21,977
And we did something that everybody said couldn't be done.
而我们做了一件每个人都说无法做到的事情。

290
00:21:22,077 --> 00:21:25,079
And now you have a vote of the people on abortion.
现在你在堕胎问题上有了人民的投票。

291
00:21:25,559 --> 00:21:32,167
Vice President Harris, I want to give you your time to respond, but I do want to ask, would you support any restrictions on a woman's right to an abortion?
哈里斯副总统，我想给你时间回应，但我想问，你会支持对女性堕胎权的任何限制吗？

292
00:21:32,527 --> 00:21:40,937
I absolutely support reinstating the protections of Roe v. Wade, and as you rightly mentioned, nowhere in America
我绝对支持恢复《罗诉韦德案》的保护，正如你所提到的，

293
00:21:41,898 --> 00:21:47,963
is a woman carrying a pregnancy to term and asking for an abortion.
在美国，没有哪个女性是怀孕到足月后才要求堕胎的。

294
00:21:48,023 --> 00:21:49,004
That is not happening.
这种情况并不存在。

295
00:21:49,044 --> 00:21:51,446
It's insulting to the women of America.
这对美国女性来说是非常侮辱的。

296
00:21:51,726 --> 00:21:55,429
And understand what has been happening under Donald Trump's abortion bans.
而且要理解在特朗普的堕胎禁令下发生了什么。

297
00:21:56,150 --> 00:22:03,896
Couples who pray and dream of having a family are being denied IVF treatments.
那些祈祷和梦想拥有家庭的夫妇被拒绝接受试管婴儿治疗。

298
00:22:04,617 --> 00:22:06,219
What is happening in our country?
我们国家发生了什么？

299
00:22:06,759 --> 00:22:24,014
Working people, working women who are working one or two jobs, who can barely afford child care as it is, have to travel to another state to get on a plane sitting next to strangers to go and get the health care she needs.
那些在工作、做一两份工作的女性，

300
00:22:25,035 --> 00:22:30,917
barely can afford to do it, and what you are putting her through is unconscionable.
她们几乎负担不起儿童保育，必须去另一个州坐飞机，和陌生人挤在一起，去获得她所需的医疗服务。

301
00:22:31,577 --> 00:22:47,723
And the people of America have not—the majority of Americans believe in a woman's right to make decisions about her own body, and that is why, in every state where this issue has been on the ballot, in red and blue states both, the people of America have voted for freedom.
美国人民并没有——大多数美国人相信女性有权对自己的身体做出决定，这就是为什么在每个州，无论是红州还是蓝州，当这个问题出现在投票上时，美国人民都投票支持自由。

302
00:22:48,359 --> 00:22:48,819
vice president
副总统

303
00:23:04,893 --> 00:23:09,295
I saw the people of Alabama and the legislature two days later voted it in.
我看到阿拉巴马州的民众和立法机关在两天后通过了这个法案。

304
00:23:09,775 --> 00:23:11,016
I've been a leader on it.
我一直是这个问题的领导者。

305
00:23:11,316 --> 00:23:13,357
They know that and everybody else knows it.
他们知道这一点，其他人也知道。

306
00:23:13,817 --> 00:23:16,398
I have been a leader on fertilization IVF.
我一直在生育治疗（IVF）方面担任领导者。

307
00:23:16,858 --> 00:23:25,102
And the other thing, they, you should ask, will she allow abortion in the eighth month, ninth month, seventh month?
还有一件事，你应该问，她会允许在第八个月、第九个月、第七个月进行堕胎吗？

308
00:23:25,622 --> 00:23:26,062
Come on.
得了吧。

309
00:23:26,082 --> 00:23:26,983
Okay, would you do that?
好吧，你会这样做吗？

310
00:23:28,314 --> 00:23:29,855
Why don't you ask her that question?
为什么不问她这个问题？

311
00:23:29,875 --> 00:23:30,896
That's the problem.
这就是问题所在。

312
00:23:30,916 --> 00:23:39,384
Because under Roe v. Wade, you could do abortions in the seventh month, the eighth month, the ninth month, and probably after birth.
因为根据《罗诉韦德案》，你可以在第七个月、第八个月、第九个月进行堕胎，甚至可能在出生后。

313
00:23:39,664 --> 00:23:42,746
Just look at the governor, former governor of Virginia.
看看弗吉尼亚州的前州长。

314
00:23:43,127 --> 00:23:48,011
The governor of Virginia said we put the baby aside and then we determine what we want to do with the baby.
弗吉尼亚州州长曾说，我们将婴儿放在一边，然后决定我们想对婴儿做什么。

315
00:23:48,031 --> 00:23:49,112
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢。

316
00:23:49,332 --> 00:23:51,833
We're going to turn now to immigration and border security.
现在我们来谈谈移民和边境安全。

317
00:23:51,873 --> 00:23:56,514
We know it's an issue that's important to Republicans, Democrats, voters across the board in this country.
我们知道这是一个对共和党、民主党以及全国各地选民都非常重要的问题。

318
00:23:57,014 --> 00:24:02,775
Vice President Harris, you were tasked by President Biden with getting to the root causes of migration from Central America.
哈里斯副总统，拜登总统让您负责解决中美洲移民的根本原因。

319
00:24:03,255 --> 00:24:07,256
We know that illegal border crossings reached a record high in the Biden administration.
我们知道在拜登政府期间，非法边境穿越达到了历史新高。

320
00:24:07,316 --> 00:24:10,977
This past June, President Biden imposed tough new asylum restrictions.
在今年六月，拜登总统实施了严格的新庇护限制。

321
00:24:11,017 --> 00:24:13,858
We know the numbers since then have dropped significantly.
我们知道自那以后，这个数字大幅下降。

322
00:24:14,298 --> 00:24:19,542
But my question to you tonight is, why did the administration wait until six months before the election to act?
但我今晚要问您的是，为什么政府在选举前六个月才采取行动？

323
00:24:19,983 --> 00:24:22,945
And would you have done anything differently from President Biden on this?
您会在这方面与拜登总统有所不同吗？

324
00:24:23,446 --> 00:24:32,213
So I'm the only person on this stage who has prosecuted transnational criminal organizations for the trafficking of guns, drugs and human beings.
所以我是这个舞台上唯一一个起诉跨国犯罪组织，涉及枪支、毒品和人口贩卖的人。

325
00:24:32,933 --> 00:24:43,141
And let me say that the United States Congress, including some of the most conservative members of the United States Senate, came up with a border security bill, which I supported.
让我说，美国国会，包括一些最保守的参议员，提出了一项边境安全法案，我支持该法案。

326
00:24:44,262 --> 00:24:53,051
And that bill would have put 1,500 more border agents on the border to help those folks who are working there right now, over time, trying to do their job.
该法案将增加1500名边境警察，以帮助那些正在努力工作的人员。

327
00:24:53,852 --> 00:24:59,058
It would have allowed us to stem the flow of fentanyl coming into the United States.
这将使我们能够遏制芬太尼进入美国的流动。

328
00:24:59,458 --> 00:25:02,982
I know there are so many families watching tonight who have been personally affected
我知道今晚有很多家庭受到芬太尼激增的影响。

329
00:25:03,462 --> 00:25:05,283
by the surge of fentanyl in our country.
该法案将提供更多资源，以便我们起诉跨国犯罪组织，涉及枪支、毒品和人口贩卖。

330
00:25:05,823 --> 00:25:14,386
That bill would have put more resources to allow us to prosecute transnational criminal organizations for trafficking in guns, drugs, and human beings.
这将使我们能够有效打击这些犯罪活动。

331
00:25:14,406 --> 00:25:16,047
But you know what happened to that bill?
但你知道那项法案发生了什么吗？

332
00:25:16,847 --> 00:25:21,709
Donald Trump got on the phone, called up some folks in Congress, and said, kill the bill.
唐纳德·特朗普给国会的一些人打了电话，要求他们阻止这项法案。

333
00:25:21,749 --> 00:25:22,469
And you know why?
你知道为什么吗？

334
00:25:23,009 --> 00:25:27,691
Because he'd prefer to run on a problem instead of fixing a problem.
因为他宁愿在一个问题上竞选，而不是去解决问题。

335
00:25:28,411 --> 00:25:41,275
And understand, this comes at a time where the people of our country actually need a leader who engages in solutions, who actually addresses the problems at hand.
而且要理解，这发生在我们国家人民实际上需要一位参与解决方案的领导者的时候，他真正解决眼前的问题。

336
00:25:41,755 --> 00:25:47,256
But what we have in the former president is someone who would prefer to run on a problem instead of fixing a problem.
但我们在前总统身上看到的是一个宁愿在一个问题上竞选，而不是去解决问题的人。

337
00:25:47,616 --> 00:25:52,478
And I'll tell you something, he's going to talk about immigration a lot tonight, even when it's not the subject that is being raised.
我告诉你，他今晚会谈论很多移民问题，即使这并不是被提出的话题。

338
00:25:53,078 --> 00:26:00,664
And I'm going to actually do something really unusual, and I'm going to invite you to attend one of Donald Trump's rallies, because it's a really interesting thing to watch.
而且我将做一件非常不寻常的事情，我邀请你去参加唐纳德·特朗普的集会，因为这是一件非常有趣的事情。

339
00:26:01,404 --> 00:26:06,168
You will see during the course of his rallies, he talks about fictional characters like Hannibal Lecter.
你会看到在他的集会期间，他谈论虚构的人物，比如汉尼拔·莱克特。

340
00:26:06,969 --> 00:26:09,451
He will talk about when mills cause cancer.
他会谈论工厂如何导致癌症。

341
00:26:10,231 --> 00:26:15,815
And what you will also notice is that people start leaving his rallies early, out of exhaustion and boredom.
你还会注意到人们开始提前离开他的集会，出于疲惫和无聊。

342
00:26:16,616 --> 00:26:19,801
And I will tell you, the one thing you will not hear him talk about is you.
我告诉你，你不会听到他谈论的是你。

343
00:26:20,422 --> 00:26:24,648
You will not hear him talk about your needs, your dreams, and your desires.
你不会听到他谈论你的需求、你的梦想和你的愿望。

344
00:26:25,229 --> 00:26:31,498
And I'll tell you, I believe you deserve a president who actually puts you first, and I pledge to you that I will.
我告诉你，我相信你值得拥有一位真正把你放在首位的总统，我向你承诺我会这样做。

345
00:26:31,778 --> 00:26:32,940
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢你。

346
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:34,642
President Trump, on that point, I want to get your response.
特朗普总统，关于这一点，我想听听你的回应。

347
00:26:34,662 --> 00:26:35,623
Well, I would like to respond.
嗯，我想回应一下。

348
00:26:35,643 --> 00:26:41,971
Let me just ask, though, why did you try to kill that bill, and successfully so, that would have put thousands of additional agents and officers on the border?
不过让我问一下，你为什么试图阻止那项法案，而且成功了，那项法案将会在边境增加数千名额外的特工和警官？

349
00:26:41,991 --> 00:26:43,653
First let me respond is to the rallies.
首先让我回应的是集会。

350
00:26:44,214 --> 00:26:45,656
She said people start leaving.
她说人们开始离开。

351
00:26:45,696 --> 00:26:46,997
People don't go to her rallies.
人们不去她的集会。

352
00:26:47,017 --> 00:26:47,878
There's no reason to go.
没有理由去。

353
00:26:48,619 --> 00:26:55,304
And the people that do go, she's bussing them in and paying them to be there, and then showing them in a different light.
而且那些去的人，她是通过巴士把他们运来的，并支付他们到场，然后以不同的方式展示他们。

354
00:26:55,764 --> 00:26:57,285
So she can't talk about that.
所以她不能谈论这个。

355
00:26:57,325 --> 00:26:58,506
People don't leave my rallies.
人们不会离开我的集会。

356
00:26:58,646 --> 00:27:02,208
We have the biggest rallies, the most incredible rallies in the history of politics.
我们拥有历史上最大的集会，最令人难以置信的集会。

357
00:27:02,508 --> 00:27:05,050
That's because people want to take their country back.
这是因为人们想要夺回他们的国家。

358
00:27:05,530 --> 00:27:07,211
Our country is being lost.
我们的国家正在失去。

359
00:27:07,251 --> 00:27:08,372
We're a failing nation.
我们是一个失败的国家。

360
00:27:08,732 --> 00:27:10,974
And it happened three and a half years ago.
这一切发生在三年半前。

361
00:27:11,594 --> 00:27:16,658
And what's going on here, you're going to end up in World War III, just to go into another subject.
而这里发生的事情是，你最终会陷入第三次世界大战，只是为了谈论另一个话题

362
00:27:17,358 --> 00:27:27,067
what they have done to our country by allowing these millions and millions of people to come into our country and look at what's happening to the towns all over the United States.
他们通过允许数以百万计的人涌入我们的国家，对我们的国家造成了什么影响，看看美国各地城镇发生的事情

363
00:27:27,107 --> 00:27:28,328
And a lot of towns don't want to talk.
很多城镇不想谈论这个

364
00:27:28,348 --> 00:27:30,109
It's not going to be Aurora or Springfield.
这不会是奥罗拉或斯普林菲尔德

365
00:27:30,550 --> 00:27:33,652
A lot of towns don't want to talk about it because they're so embarrassed by it.
很多城镇不想谈论这件事，因为他们对此感到非常尴尬

366
00:27:34,233 --> 00:27:38,536
In Springfield, they're eating the dogs, the people that came in.
在斯普林菲尔德，刚来的人在吃狗

367
00:27:38,797 --> 00:27:39,938
They're eating the cats.
他们在吃猫

368
00:27:40,178 --> 00:27:40,758
They're eating
他们在吃

369
00:27:41,619 --> 00:27:45,522
They're eating the pets of the people that live there.
他们在吃当地居民的宠物

370
00:27:46,023 --> 00:27:48,165
And this is what's happening in our country.
这就是我们国家发生的事情

371
00:27:48,525 --> 00:27:49,346
And it's a shame.
这真是个耻辱

372
00:27:49,786 --> 00:27:55,551
As far as rallies are concerned, as far as — the reason they go is they like what I say.
至于集会，至于——他们去的原因是他们喜欢我说的话

373
00:27:55,851 --> 00:27:57,633
They want to bring our country back.
他们想要让我们的国家回归

374
00:27:57,873 --> 00:27:59,615
They want to make America great again.
他们想让美国再次伟大

375
00:27:59,635 --> 00:28:02,157
It's a very simple phrase — make America great again.
这是一个非常简单的短语——让美国再次伟大

376
00:28:02,777 --> 00:28:08,838
She's destroying this country, and if she becomes president, this country doesn't have a chance of success.
她正在摧毁这个国家，如果她成为总统，这个国家就没有成功的机会

377
00:28:09,218 --> 00:28:13,219
Not only success, we'll end up being Venezuela on steroids.
不仅仅是成功，我们最终会变成超级委内瑞拉

378
00:28:13,979 --> 00:28:14,919
I just want to clarify here.
我只是想澄清一下

379
00:28:14,939 --> 00:28:19,780
You bring up Springfield, Ohio, and ABC News did reach out to the city manager there.
你提到斯普林菲尔德，俄亥俄州，ABC新闻确实联系了那里的城市经理

380
00:28:19,820 --> 00:28:27,642
He told us there had been no credible reports of specific claims of pets being harmed, injured, or abused by individuals within the immigrant community.
他告诉我们，没有可信的报告显示移民社区内的个人对宠物造成了伤害、受伤或虐待

381
00:28:27,662 --> 00:28:28,862
Well, I've seen people on television.
好吧，我在电视上看到过人们

382
00:28:29,862 --> 00:28:33,904
The people on television say my dog was taken and used for food.
电视上的人说我的狗被拿走了，用来当食物

383
00:28:34,004 --> 00:28:37,845
So maybe he said that, and maybe that's a good thing to say for a city manager.
所以也许他说过这个，或许这对城市经理来说是个好说法

384
00:28:37,905 --> 00:28:39,165
I'm not taking this from television.
我不是从电视上获取这些信息

385
00:28:39,185 --> 00:28:43,587
But the people on television say my dog was eaten by the people that went there.
但电视上的人说我的狗被那些去那儿的人吃了

386
00:28:44,427 --> 00:28:46,768
Again, the Springfield city manager says there's no evidence of that.
再次强调，斯普林菲尔德的城市经理表示没有证据支持这一点

387
00:28:46,848 --> 00:28:49,029
Vice President Harris, I'll let you respond to the rest of what you've heard.
哈里斯副总统，我让你回应你所听到的其他内容

388
00:28:50,077 --> 00:28:51,538
You talk about extreme.
你谈到极端

389
00:28:54,939 --> 00:29:15,088
This is, I think, one of the reasons why, in this election, I actually have the endorsement of 200 Republicans who have formally worked with President Bush, Mitt Romney, and John McCain, including the endorsement of former Vice President Dick Cheney and Congress member Liz Cheney.
我认为这也是为什么在这次选举中，我实际上得到了200名与布什总统、米特·罗姆尼和约翰·麦凯恩正式合作的共和党人的支持，包括前副总统迪克·切尼和国会议员莉兹·切尼的支持

390
00:29:16,028 --> 00:29:25,396
And if you want to really know the inside track on who the former president is, if he didn't make it clear already, just ask people who have worked with him.
如果你真的想知道前总统的内幕，假如他还没有明确表明，只需问那些与他合作过的人

391
00:29:25,997 --> 00:29:31,882
His former chief of staff, a four-star general, has said he has contempt for the Constitution of the United States.
他之前的首席幕僚，一个四星将军，曾表示他对美国宪法充满蔑视。

392
00:29:32,623 --> 00:29:36,546
His former national security advisor has said he is dangerous and unfit.
他之前的国家安全顾问曾说他是危险且不适合的人。

393
00:29:37,447 --> 00:29:45,772
His former Secretary of Defense has said the nation, the republic, would never survive another Trump term.
他之前的国防部长曾表示，国家和共和国在特朗普的第二个任期中绝对无法存活。

394
00:29:46,832 --> 00:29:57,038
And when we listen to this kind of rhetoric, when the issues that affect the American people are not being addressed, I think the choice is clear in this election.
当我们听到这种言论时，影响美国人民的问题没有得到解决，我认为这次选举的选择是明确的。

395
00:29:57,478 --> 00:29:59,259
President Trump will give you a quick minute to respond.
总统特朗普会给你一分钟的时间回应。

396
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:00,940
Thank you.
谢谢。

397
00:30:01,161 --> 00:30:04,763
Because when I hear that, see, I'm a different kind of a person.
因为当我听到这些，我就会发现，我是一个不同类型的人。

398
00:30:05,103 --> 00:30:06,744
I fired most of those people.
我解雇了大多数那些人。

399
00:30:07,565 --> 00:30:08,445
Not so graciously.
并不是那么优雅。

400
00:30:08,485 --> 00:30:10,567
They did bad things or a bad job.
他们做了坏事或者工作表现差。

401
00:30:10,987 --> 00:30:11,467
I fired them.
我解雇了他们。

402
00:30:11,688 --> 00:30:13,049
They never fired one person.
他们从来没有解雇过一个人。

403
00:30:13,369 --> 00:30:19,373
They didn't fire anybody having to do with Afghanistan and the Taliban and the 13 people who's who's
他们没有解雇任何与阿富汗和塔利班有关的人，以及那13个

404
00:30:19,873 --> 00:30:22,494
were just killed, viciously and violently killed.
被残忍而暴力地杀害的人。

405
00:30:22,554 --> 00:30:24,495
And I got to know the parents and the family.
我认识了那些父母和家庭。

406
00:30:25,055 --> 00:30:25,676
They didn't fire.
他们没有解雇。

407
00:30:25,716 --> 00:30:34,380
They should have fired all those generals, all those top people, because that was one of the most incompetently handled situations anybody has ever seen.
他们应该解雇所有那些将军，所有那些高层，因为那是有史以来处理得最无能的局面之一。

408
00:30:34,820 --> 00:30:38,041
So when somebody does a bad job, I fire him.
所以当有人工作表现差时，我就解雇他。

409
00:30:38,461 --> 00:30:40,002
And you take a guy like Esper.
你看像埃斯珀这样的家伙。

410
00:30:40,062 --> 00:30:40,742
He was no good.
他不好。

411
00:30:40,802 --> 00:30:41,383
I fired him.
我解雇了他。

412
00:30:41,423 --> 00:30:42,243
So he writes a book.
所以他写了一本书。

413
00:30:42,323 --> 00:30:43,384
Another one writes a book.
另一个人也写了一本书。

414
00:30:43,464 --> 00:30:44,804
Because with me, they can write books.
因为在我这里，他们可以写书。

415
00:30:44,824 --> 00:30:45,865
With nobody else can they.
而在其他人那里，他们不能。

416
00:30:46,445 --> 00:30:51,008
But they have done such a poor job, and they never fire anybody.
但他们做得如此糟糕，他们从来没有解雇任何人。

417
00:30:51,368 --> 00:30:52,408
Look at the economy.
看看经济。

418
00:30:52,448 --> 00:30:53,869
Look at the inflation.
看看通货膨胀。

419
00:30:54,109 --> 00:30:56,291
They didn't fire any of their economists.
他们没有解雇任何他们的经济学家。

420
00:30:56,311 --> 00:30:57,311
They have the same people.
他们还是那些人。

421
00:30:57,571 --> 00:31:00,373
That's a good way not to have books written about you.
这是一种不会让人写关于你的书的好方法。

422
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:06,216
But just to finish, I got more votes than any Republican in history by far.
不过我想补充一点，我获得的选票比历史上任何一位共和党人都要多得多。

423
00:31:07,357 --> 00:31:12,740
In fact, I got more votes than any president, sitting president, in history by far.
事实上，我获得的选票比历史上任何一位在任总统都要多得多。

424
00:31:14,212 --> 00:31:15,353
Let me continue on immigration.
让我继续谈谈移民问题。

425
00:31:15,373 --> 00:31:16,814
It was what you wanted to talk about earlier.
这是你之前想讨论的主题。

426
00:31:16,874 --> 00:31:22,719
So let's get back to your deportation proposal that the vice president has reacted to as well.
所以让我们回到副总统对此做出的反应的驱逐提案。

427
00:31:23,239 --> 00:31:27,583
President Trump, you call this the largest domestic deportation operation in the history of our country.
特朗普总统，您称这是我们国家历史上最大规模的国内驱逐行动。

428
00:31:27,623 --> 00:31:29,204
You say you would use the National Guard.
您说您会动用国民警卫队。

429
00:31:29,244 --> 00:31:32,287
You say if things get out of control, you'd have no problem using the U.S.
您说如果局势失控，您不会介意使用美国

430
00:31:32,347 --> 00:31:32,967
military.
军队。

431
00:31:33,468 --> 00:31:35,289
You also said you would use local police.
您还说您会利用地方警察。

432
00:31:36,150 --> 00:31:39,413
How would you deport 11 million undocumented immigrants?
您将如何驱逐1100万无证移民？

433
00:31:39,433 --> 00:31:41,734
I know you believe that number is much higher.
我知道您认为这个数字要高得多。

434
00:31:42,475 --> 00:31:43,156
Take us through this.
请给我们详细讲讲。

435
00:31:43,236 --> 00:31:44,136
What does this look like?
这会是什么样子？

436
00:31:44,156 --> 00:31:46,018
Will authorities be going door to door in this country?
当局会在这个国家挨家挨户地去吗？

437
00:31:46,118 --> 00:31:49,161
Yeah, it is much higher because of them.
是的，确实要高得多，因为他们。

438
00:31:49,681 --> 00:31:52,904
They allowed criminals, many, many millions of criminals.
他们允许罪犯，许多、许多的罪犯。

439
00:31:53,484 --> 00:31:54,525
They allowed terrorists.
他们允许恐怖分子。

440
00:31:54,625 --> 00:31:57,047
They allowed common street criminals.
他们允许普通街头罪犯。

441
00:31:57,107 --> 00:32:00,430
They allowed people to come in, drug dealers to come into our country.
他们允许毒贩进入我们的国家。

442
00:32:00,450 --> 00:32:05,775
And then now in the United States and told by their countries like Venezuela,
而现在在美国，被他们的国家像委内瑞拉

443
00:32:06,115 --> 00:32:08,456
Don't ever come back or we're going to kill you.
告知，永远不要回来，否则我们会杀了你。

444
00:32:08,757 --> 00:32:14,540
Do you know that crime in Venezuela and crime in countries all over the world is way down?
你知道委内瑞拉和世界各地的犯罪率都大幅下降吗？

445
00:32:14,560 --> 00:32:15,560
You know why?
你知道为什么吗？

446
00:32:15,881 --> 00:32:20,943
Because they've taken their criminals off the street and they've given them to her to put into our country.
因为他们将街上的罪犯抓走，交给她放进我们的国家。

447
00:32:21,444 --> 00:32:30,549
And this will be one of the greatest mistakes in history for them to allow, and I think they probably did it because they think they're going to get votes, but it's not worth it.
这将是历史上最大的错误之一，他们允许这样做，我认为他们可能是因为认为能得到选票，但这不值得。

448
00:32:31,109 --> 00:32:35,130
because they're destroying the fabric of our country by what they've done.
因为他们通过所做的事情正在摧毁我们国家的基础。

449
00:32:35,390 --> 00:32:38,111
There's never been anything done like this at all.
从来没有任何事情像这样发生过。

450
00:32:38,131 --> 00:32:40,612
They've destroyed the fabric of our country.
他们摧毁了我们国家的基础。

451
00:32:41,112 --> 00:32:42,733
Millions of people let in.
数百万人被允许入境。

452
00:32:42,993 --> 00:32:46,894
And all over the world, crime is down all over the world except here.
而在全球范围内，犯罪率在下降，除了这里。

453
00:32:47,175 --> 00:32:49,155
Crime here is up and through the roof.
这里的犯罪率上升，严重失控。

454
00:32:49,455 --> 00:32:54,257
Despite their fraudulent statements that they made, crime in this country is through the roof.
尽管他们发表了虚假的声明，但这个国家的犯罪率确实失控了。

455
00:32:54,537 --> 00:32:55,898
And we have a new form of crime.
我们出现了一种新的犯罪形式。

456
00:32:55,938 --> 00:32:57,278
It's called migrant crime.
这被称为移民犯罪。

457
00:32:57,558 --> 00:33:00,139
And it's happening at levels that nobody thought possible.
这种情况的发生率是没人想到的。

458
00:33:00,179 --> 00:33:07,643
President Trump, as you know, the FBI says overall violent crime is actually coming down in this country, but Vice President Harris... Excuse me, the FBI defraud... They were defrauding statements.
特朗普总统，正如您所知，联邦调查局表示该国的暴力犯罪总体上实际上在下降，但哈里斯副总统……抱歉，联邦调查局的声明是虚假的。

459
00:33:07,983 --> 00:33:10,124
They didn't include the worst cities.
他们没有包括最糟糕的城市。

460
00:33:10,445 --> 00:33:13,086
They didn't include the cities with the worst crime.
他们没有包括犯罪率最高的城市。

461
00:33:13,446 --> 00:33:20,190
It was a fraud, just like their number of 818,000 jobs that they said they created turned out to be a fraud.
这是一场欺诈，就像他们声称创造的818,000个工作岗位，结果也被证明是欺诈。

462
00:33:20,210 --> 00:33:20,990
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢。

463
00:33:21,010 --> 00:33:22,171
I'll let you respond, Vice President Harris.
我让您回应，哈里斯副总统。

464
00:33:22,191 --> 00:33:26,953
Well, I think this is so rich, coming from someone who has been prosecuted.
嗯，我觉得这真是太可笑了，来自一个被起诉的人。

465
00:33:28,294 --> 00:33:43,939
for national security crimes, economic crimes, election interference, has been found liable for sexual assault, and his next big court appearance is in November at his own criminal sentencing.
因国家安全犯罪、经济犯罪、选举干预而被起诉，因性侵犯被判定有罪，而他下一个重要的法庭出庭时间是在11月，进行自己的刑事判决。

466
00:33:44,778 --> 00:33:54,360
And let's be clear where each person stands on the issue of what is important about respect for the rule of law and respect for law enforcement.
让我们明确每个人在法治和执法尊重问题上的立场。

467
00:33:54,680 --> 00:34:05,163
The former vice president called for defunding federal law enforcement, 45,000 agents, get this, on the day after he was arraigned on 34 felony counts.
前副总统呼吁削减联邦执法拨款，4.5万名特工，听着，就在他因34项重罪被起诉的第二天。

468
00:34:07,023 --> 00:34:10,324
So let's talk about what is important in this race.
那么，让我们谈谈这场竞选中重要的事情。

469
00:34:10,464 --> 00:34:32,150
It is important that we move forward, that we turn the page on this same old tired rhetoric and address the needs of the American people, address what we need to do about the housing shortage, which I have a plan for, address what we must do to support our small businesses, address bringing down the price of groceries.
重要的是我们要向前推进，翻开这一套陈旧的说辞，解决美国人民的需求，解决我们在住房短缺方面需要做的事情，我有一个计划，解决我们必须做的支持小企业的问题，解决降低食品价格的问题。

470
00:34:32,890 --> 00:34:37,713
But, frankly, the American people are exhausted with the same old tired playbook.
但坦率地说，美国人民对这一套陈旧的剧本感到疲惫。

471
00:34:38,053 --> 00:34:39,354
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢。

472
00:34:39,534 --> 00:34:39,995
Excuse me.
抱歉。

473
00:34:40,575 --> 00:34:45,178
Every one of those cases was started by them against their political opponent.
每一个案件都是由他们针对自己的政治对手发起的。

474
00:34:45,558 --> 00:34:48,340
And I'm winning most of them, and I will win the rest on appeal.
我赢了大部分案件，我将在上诉中赢得其余案件。

475
00:34:48,781 --> 00:34:52,543
And you saw that with the decision that came down just recently from the Supreme Court.
您可以看到，刚刚从最高法院下达的判决就是一个例子。

476
00:34:52,943 --> 00:34:53,864
I'm winning most of them.
我赢了大部分案件。

477
00:34:54,144 --> 00:34:58,287
But those are cases, it's called weaponization, never happened in this country.
但这些案件，被称为武器化，在这个国家从未发生过。

478
00:34:58,647 --> 00:35:00,688
They weaponized the Justice Department.
他们将司法部武器化了。

479
00:35:00,888 --> 00:35:10,794
Every one of those cases was involved with the DOJ, from Atlanta and Fawny Willis to the Attorney General of New York and the DA in New York.
每一个案件都涉及司法部，从亚特兰大和福尼·威利斯到纽约的检察总长和地区检察官。

480
00:35:11,274 --> 00:35:12,575
Every one of those cases.
每一个案件。

481
00:35:13,095 --> 00:35:16,497
And then they say, oh, he's a criminal.
然后他们说，哦，他是个罪犯。

482
00:35:16,737 --> 00:35:19,759
They're the ones that made them go after me.
是他们让人追究我的。

483
00:35:19,819 --> 00:35:24,001
By the way, Joe Biden was found essentially guilty on the documents case.
顺便说一句，乔·拜登在文件案件中基本上被判有罪。

484
00:35:24,022 --> 00:35:25,983
Now, what happened in my documents case?
那么，我的文件案件发生了什么？

485
00:35:26,263 --> 00:35:27,904
They said, oh, that's the toughest of them all.
他们说，哦，那是所有案件中最棘手的。

486
00:35:28,564 --> 00:35:30,666
a complete and total victory.
这是一个完全的胜利。

487
00:35:30,726 --> 00:35:32,488
Two months ago, it was thrown out.
两个月前，这个案件被驳回了。

488
00:35:33,349 --> 00:35:36,872
It's weaponization, and they used it, and it's never happened in this country.
这是武器化，他们利用它，这在这个国家从未发生过。

489
00:35:37,313 --> 00:35:39,795
They used it to try and win an election.
他们用它来试图赢得选举。

490
00:35:39,875 --> 00:35:41,177
They're fake cases.
这些都是虚假的案件。

